WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.480
Test 3.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.280
This is the IELTS listening test.

3
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:16.300
You will hear a number of different recordings and you will have to answer questions on what you hear.

4
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:24.260
There will be time for you to read the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work.

5
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.300
All the recordings will be played once only.

6
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.400
The test is in four parts.

7
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:38.780
At the end of the test, you will be given ten minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet.

8
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.540
Now turn to part one.

9
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.340
Part one.

10
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:57.300
You will hear a woman phoning the owner of a house she is going to rent about companies that she could rent furniture from.

11
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.500
First, you have some time to look at questions one to five.

12
00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.090
Now listen carefully and answer questions one to five.

13
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.380
<v LANDLORD> Good morning.

14
00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.980
<v SHELLEY> Hi, this is Shelley Meyer.

15
00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.760
<v SHELLEY> I'm renting your house on Archwood Avenue.

16
00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.020
<v SHELLEY> I'm due to move in next week.

17
00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.200
<v LANDLORD> Oh yes, hello Ms. Meyer.

18
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.700
<v LANDLORD> What can I do for you?

19
00:01:53.220 --> 00:02:02.880
<v SHELLEY> When I viewed the house, I told you I'll most probably need to rent some furniture, at least until I know whether my temporary work contract is going to be made permanent.

20
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.100
<v LANDLORD> Yes, of course, I remember.

21
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:10.360
<v LANDLORD> And I said I could give you some information about furniture rental companies in the city.

22
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:11.620
<v SHELLEY> That's right.

23
00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.400
<v LANDLORD> Well, the biggest company is called Peak Rentals.

24
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.200
<v LANDLORD> I've recommended them to other people and have always heard positive reports about them.

25
00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.140
<v SHELLEY> Could you give me an idea of their costs?

26
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:24.300
<v LANDLORD> Sure.

27
00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.980
<v LANDLORD> I actually have one of their brochures here.

28
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:34.840
<v LANDLORD> It says the monthly price per room starts at $105 and goes up to $239.

29
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.300
<v LANDLORD> That depends on which rooms you need furniture for, of course.

30
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.220
<v SHELLEY> Sure.

31
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.220
<v SHELLEY> It's just to get a general idea of how much it's going to cost.

32
00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.820
<v SHELLEY> And you said you had some positive feedback about this company?

33
00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:49.860
<v LANDLORD> Yes.

34
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:56.240
<v LANDLORD> People have mentioned that the furniture from Peak Rentals is more modern than any of the other companies.

35
00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:03.540
<v LANDLORD> And also, once you place an order, the furniture will be delivered to you in just one or two days.

36
00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.520
<v SHELLEY> That would be really helpful.

37
00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:10.640
<v LANDLORD> Oh, and the brochure says that there's a special offer at the moment.

38
00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:20.340
<v LANDLORD> If you rent living room furniture, I believe that's a set of chairs and a TV table, you'll also get a lamp at no extra cost.

39
00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:26.600
<v SHELLEY> Okay, but you know, that price range you gave is more than I was hoping to pay.

40
00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.700
<v LANDLORD> Then you could try Aaron and Oliver.

41
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:30.520
<v SHELLEY> Sorry.

42
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.920
<v SHELLEY> What and Oliver?

43
00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.040
<v LANDLORD> Aaron.

44
00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.260
<v LANDLORD> Double A-R-O-N.

45
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:37.600
<v SHELLEY> Okay.

46
00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.360
<v SHELLEY> Are they cheaper?

47
00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.240
<v LANDLORD> I'd say they're a mid-price company.

48
00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:49.280
<v LANDLORD> But if you chose them, you need to be aware that they charge an extra 12% every month in case of damage.

49
00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.320
<v SHELLEY> Oh, I see.

50
00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.080
<v SHELLEY> I'd have to do the math carefully then.

51
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:54.820
<v LANDLORD> Right.

52
00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.360
<v LANDLORD> But one helpful thing is that they also do cleaning for customers.

53
00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.580
<v SHELLEY> For the furniture?

54
00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.020
<v LANDLORD> For the house.

55
00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.360
<v SHELLEY> Oh, I see.

56
00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.360
<v SHELLEY> I probably won't need that.

57
00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:14.930
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions six to ten.

58
00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:53.450
Now listen and answer questions six to ten.

59
00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.940
<v LANDLORD> There's another company called Larch Furniture.

60
00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.920
<v LANDLORD> It's quite new and it has the lowest prices in town.

61
00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:08.120
<v LANDLORD> That's for both furniture and also electronic equipment.

62
00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.080
<v SHELLEY> Well, that would be good.

63
00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:17.160
<v SHELLEY> I'm not bringing much with me and I won't have much time to go shopping after I start my job.

64
00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:21.240
<v LANDLORD> There are two things you need to know about Larch Furniture.

65
00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:27.580
<v LANDLORD> First of all, you have to take out insurance on the furniture and you need to organize that yourself.

66
00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.220
<v SHELLEY> That wouldn't be too hard.

67
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.860
<v LANDLORD> Also, you can't take out a contract for less than six months.

68
00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.120
<v LANDLORD> But I figure that might not be a problem for you.

69
00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.880
<v LANDLORD> You're renting the house for 12 months after all, aren't you?

70
00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.200
<v SHELLEY> Yes, okay, well...

71
00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.100
<v LANDLORD> Sorry to interrupt.

72
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.160
<v LANDLORD> I just thought of another furniture rental company.

73
00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:53.200
<v LANDLORD> It's called Space Rentals and it's located very near to the house.

74
00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:54.180
<v SHELLEY> Okay.

75
00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:03.020
<v LANDLORD> I don't have any information about their charges, so it's best to use their app to find out what it would cost you to use them.

76
00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.380
<v SHELLEY> Okay, thanks.

77
00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.300
<v SHELLEY> I'll do that.

78
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:16.120
<v LANDLORD> One good thing about that company is that if you don't like the furniture once it's delivered, you can request exchanges, as long as you do that within a week of receiving it.

79
00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.580
<v SHELLEY> That sounds really great.

80
00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:21.840
<v SHELLEY> Okay, well, thanks very much.

81
00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.240
<v SHELLEY> That's so helpful.

82
00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.960
That is the end of Part 1.

83
00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:33.740
You now have one minute to check your answers to Part 1.
